home='''<section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">TABLETOP GAMING / VETERAN-FOCUSED COMMUNITY</p><h1>Tabletop play.<br>A shared<br><span>purpose.</span></h1><p class="lead">Bring your best team. Pull up a chair. Be part of a community where competition, camaraderie and veteran support share the same table.</p><div class="actions">'''+a('View the next event','events.html')+'''<a class="text-link" href="about.html">Meet Red White and Clix →</a></div><div class="hero-date"><span class="small-square" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>NOV 7–8, 2026</strong><span>Lafayette, Indiana</span></div></div><figure class="hero-photo"><img src="assets/images/community-tables.jpg" alt="Players gathered around tables for miniatures games in a community game room" width="960" height="720" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption><span>THE COMMUNITY IN PLAY</span><strong>A shared table.<br>A place to belong.</strong><small>Archive photograph · context and reuse permission pending</small></figcaption></figure></section><div class="ticker"><div class="wrap"><span>PLAY WITH PURPOSE</span><span>WELCOME GENEROUSLY</span><span>COMPETE WITH RESPECT</span></div></div><section class="section wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE NEXT GATHERING</p><h2>One weekend.<br>More ways to play.</h2></div><p>November 7–8, 2026.<br>Lafayette National Guard Armory.<br>Get the details before making your plans.</p></div>'''+eventcards()+'''</section><section class="mission-section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND PEOPLE</p><h2>The game brings us in.<br>The community<br>brings us back.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Red White and Clix brings players, veterans, families and supporters together through organized tabletop events.</p><p>Our mission is to create camaraderie, raise awareness and support veteran-focused causes. We believe the next step should be clear—and there should be a welcoming seat at the table.</p><a class="text-link" href="about.html">Read our story →</a></div></div></section><section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">TAKE PART</p><h2>You bring something<br>to the table.</h2><div class="participation"><article><span class="number">01 / PLAY</span><h3>Make your next move.</h3><p>Find your format and review the event information.</p><a href="events.html">Explore the weekend →</a></article><article><span class="number">02 / SUPPORT</span><h3>Stand behind the mission.</h3><p>Learn what giving supports and how to ask about sponsorship.</p><a href="donate.html">Explore ways to support →</a></article><article><span class="number">03 / VOLUNTEER</span><h3>Help the gathering happen.</h3><p>Ask about available roles and the team behind the tables.</p><a href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=Volunteering%20with%20RWC">Ask about volunteering →</a></article></div></section>'''+cta()
render('index.html','Tabletop play. A shared purpose.','Discover veteran-founded tabletop events, community and ways to take part with Red White and Clix.',home)
events='''<section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">NOVEMBER 7–8, 2026 / LAFAYETTE, INDIANA</p><h1>Your next<br><span>seat at the table.</span></h1><p class="lead">Two days of HeroClix, a shared community and a veteran-focused purpose. Choose a format and review the details before registering.</p><nav class="section-links" aria-label="Event sections"><a href="#modern">300 Modern</a><a href="#team-sealed">Team Sealed</a><a href="#venue">Plan your visit</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav></section><div class="event-location"><div class="wrap"><strong>Lafayette National Guard Armory</strong><span>5218 Haggerty Lane · Lafayette, IN 47905</span></div></div><section class="section wrap event-detail" id="modern"><div><p class="eyebrow">SATURDAY / NOVEMBER 7</p><h2>RWC 300 Modern</h2><p>Bring your best team—and your best sportsmanship. Review the current format rules and registration information before making your plans.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=300%20Modern%20event%20question">Ask about 300 Modern →</a></div><div class="details-card"><h3>Saturday at a glance</h3><dl><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>November 7, 2026</dd></div><div><dt>Venue</dt><dd>Lafayette National Guard Armory</dd></div><div><dt>Check-in / start</dt><dd class="pending">To be confirmed</dd></div><div><dt>Entry fee</dt><dd class="pending">Amount and fee basis pending</dd></div><div><dt>Rules / refunds</dt><dd class="pending">Organizer confirmation needed</dd></div></dl><button type="button" class="button" disabled>Registration link pending</button><p class="helper">The checkout destination and fee will appear here once confirmed.</p></div></section><section class="section wrap event-detail bordered" id="team-sealed"><div><p class="eyebrow">SUNDAY / NOVEMBER 8</p><h2>Team Sealed.<br>Three players.<br>Shared purpose.</h2><p>Gather your team for the 3v3 event. Confirm the team rules, sealed-product details and fee basis with the organizer.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=Team%20Sealed%20event%20question">Ask about Team Sealed →</a></div><div class="details-card"><h3>Sunday at a glance</h3><dl><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>November 8, 2026</dd></div><div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Team Sealed · 3v3</dd></div><div><dt>Check-in / start</dt><dd class="pending">To be confirmed</dd></div><div><dt>Entry fee</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm amount and per-team or per-person basis</dd></div><div><dt>Rules / refunds</dt><dd class="pending">Organizer confirmation needed</dd></div></dl><button type="button" class="button" disabled>Registration link pending</button><p class="helper">Team purchases and individual players will be counted separately.</p></div></section><section class="mission-section" id="venue"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLAN YOUR VISIT</p><h2>Meet us<br>in Lafayette.</h2><p>Lafayette National Guard Armory<br>5218 Haggerty Lane<br>Lafayette, Indiana 47905</p><p class="helper">This is the event venue, not the organization’s permanent office.</p></div><div class="details-card"><h3>Before you travel</h3><ul class="checklist"><li>Confirm check-in and start times, including timezone.</li><li>Ask about parking, accessibility and venue entry.</li><li>Review any hotel offer and its booking deadline.</li><li>Check format requirements and refund terms.</li></ul><p class="pending">Travel and access details are awaiting organizer confirmation.</p></div></div></section><section class="section wrap narrow" id="questions"><p class="eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS. CLEAR ANSWERS.</p><h2>Before you take a seat.</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I register?</summary><p>The authoritative checkout and fee for each format are being confirmed. Contact the organizer for current registration details.</p></details><details><summary>What if I’m new to HeroClix?</summary><p>Start by reviewing the format and required game materials. Bring your questions and ask the organizer what beginner support is available. Coaching, loaners and separate beginner divisions are not yet confirmed.</p></details><details><summary>Who can answer an event question?</summary><p>Email <a href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com">redwhiteandclix@gmail.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+15742659585">574-265-9585</a>.</p></details></div></section>'''
render('events.html','November event weekend','Explore the recorded November 7–8, 2026 RWC event weekend, formats, venue and registration questions.',events)
about='''<section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">OUR STORY / RED WHITE AND CLIX</p><h1>Veteran-founded.<br><span>Community-powered.</span></h1><p class="lead">A shared hobby. A welcoming table. A practical way to stand with veterans.</p></section><section class="story wrap"><figure><img src="assets/images/community-tables.jpg" width="960" height="720" alt="Community members playing miniatures games together at tables"><figcaption>Documentary archive image · context and reuse permission pending.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY WE GATHER</p><h2>Connection begins<br>with taking part.</h2><p>Wesley Robertson created Red White and Clix to connect the camaraderie of tabletop gaming with a practical commitment to veteran support.</p><p>The community brings players, veterans, families and supporters together through organized events rooted in Indiana and open to the wider Midwest.</p><p>Serious play and a welcoming atmosphere belong at the same table.</p></div></section><section class="mission-section"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">OUR MISSION</p><h2 class="mission-statement">Bring people together through well-run tabletop gaming events that create camaraderie, raise awareness and support veteran-focused causes.</h2></div></section><section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT GUIDES US</p><h2>A community you<br>can participate in.</h2><div class="participation"><article><span class="number">01 / BELONGING</span><h3>A welcoming seat.</h3><p>Newcomers, regular players, veterans and families all have a place in the community.</p></article><article><span class="number">02 / FAIR PLAY</span><h3>Competition with respect.</h3><p>The experience should be organized, enjoyable and grounded in good sportsmanship.</p></article><article><span class="number">03 / TRANSPARENCY</span><h3>Purpose you can understand.</h3><p>Support should be explained through confirmed relationships, clear allocation and documented results.</p></article></div></section>'''+cta()
render('about.html','Our story','Meet Red White and Clix, a veteran-founded tabletop community rooted in Indiana.',about)
donate='''<section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">SUPPORT THE COMMUNITY</p><h1>Put purpose<br><span>behind every table.</span></h1><p class="lead">Support Red White and Clix and its veteran-focused mission. Understand what your gift supports before you give.</p></section><section class="section wrap giving-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">CLEAR PURPOSE. ACCOUNTABLE SUPPORT.</p><h2>Know where<br>your support goes.</h2><p>Giving information should make the beneficiary, allocation and reporting clear. Those details are being confirmed for this event.</p><div class="fact-block"><h3>Beneficiary relationship</h3><p class="pending">Confirmed organization and approved relationship description pending.</p></div><div class="fact-block"><h3>Allocation and expenses</h3><p class="pending">Event expenses, program support and transfer terms pending.</p></div><div class="fact-block"><h3>Reported results</h3><p class="pending">Verified totals, reporting period and source pending.</p></div></div><aside class="giving-card"><p class="eyebrow inverse">YOUR SUPPORT MATTERS</p><h2>Make an<br>informed gift.</h2><p>The donation recipient, checkout destination and receipt process will be shown here when confirmed.</p><button class="button" disabled>Donation link pending</button><a href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=Question%20about%20donating">Ask a giving question →</a><p class="helper">No payment information is collected in this preview.</p></aside></section><section class="mission-section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">MORE WAYS TO TAKE PART</p><h2>Time. Expertise.<br>Community support.</h2></div><div class="rwc-stack"><h3>Ask about sponsorship</h3><p>Discuss available opportunities, benefits and the event context before making a commitment.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=Sponsorship%20inquiry">Start a sponsorship conversation →</a><h3>Ask about volunteering</h3><p>Find out which roles, dates and responsibilities need support.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:redwhiteandclix@gmail.com?subject=Volunteer%20inquiry">Explore volunteer opportunities →</a></div></div></section><section class="section wrap narrow"><p class="eyebrow">GIVING QUESTIONS</p><h2>Clarity comes first.</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who issues my receipt?</summary><p>The recipient organization, receipt process and timing need confirmation before a giving link is published.</p></details><details><summary>Does every dollar go to a beneficiary?</summary><p>No allocation claim is made here. Event expenses, program support and beneficiary transfers must be documented before those statements are published.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I read an impact report?</summary><p>A report link will be added once the results, reporting period and underlying records are confirmed.</p></details></div></section>'''
render('donate.html','Support the mission','Explore ways to support Red White and Clix and the giving information that needs confirmation.',donate)
review='''<section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">INTERNAL REVIEW / NOT A LIVE SITE</p><h1>Four pages.<br><span>One clear journey.</span></h1><p class="lead">Review the visual hierarchy, wording and movement from the homepage to the event details. This static preview leaves platform choice open.</p></section><section class="section wrap narrow"><h2>What works here</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Four linked pages: home, events, our story and giving.</li><li>Responsive desktop/mobile layouts and navigation.</li><li>Event section links, email/phone links and native FAQ disclosures.</li><li>Local fonts, the supplied primary logo and documentary photo references.</li></ul><h2>What still needs a decision</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Platform, implementation scope/budget, timing and maintenance owner.</li><li>Event fees and fee basis, checkout links, check-in/start times and timezone, rules, refunds, availability and venue access.</li><li>Beneficiary relationships, allocation, donation recipient and receipts.</li><li>Photo context/permission and final content sign-off.</li><li>Traffic baseline, definition of the 80-registration goal and completed-payment reporting.</li></ul><div class="review-note"><strong>Sources and limitations</strong><p>Dates, venue and contact details are carried from the repository’s September 21, 2026 research. They were not reverified live during this preview build. Registration and donation controls are intentionally disabled until authoritative destinations are supplied.</p><p>Resource and shop links lead to the existing external website. This preview makes no production account changes, collects no form/payment information and contains no analytics integration.</p></div><h2>Review sequence</h2><ol class="checklist"><li>Start on Home, then open each event card.</li><li>Check whether the event information answers the questions needed to register.</li><li>Read Our story and the giving-page structure.</li><li>Try the mobile menu and FAQ disclosures at phone width.</li><li>Record feedback against the appropriate page before implementation.</li></ol>'''+a('Start with the homepage','index.html')+'</section>'
render('review.html','Review notes','Review notes and unresolved decisions for the local website prototype.',review)
print('Built four core pages and internal review notes.')
